ou'd like to chat about supporting us please contact our [Partnerships team](mailto:admin@computinghistory.org.uk).\n\nAll individual donations can also be Gift Aided, allowing us to claim an extra 25p on every £1 donated. [Visit our Gift Aid page](https://www.computinghistory.org.uk/pages/36973/Donate-by-BACS/) to complete a Gift Aid declaration.\n\nPlease be assured that any amount you feel able to donate will make an immediate and significant impact.\n\n|  |\n| --- |\n|  |\n\n ", "id": "0c25a5-01"}, {"url": "https://www.intc.com/stock-info/faq", "title": "FAQ :: Intel Corporation (INTC)", "score": 0.78866494, "raw_content": "# [Intel Corporation](/)\n\n# FAQ\n\n**What are Intel's ticker and CUSIP?**\n:   Intel's stock symbol is INTC  \n    Intel common stock is traded on the NASDAQ Global Select Market  \n    Our fiscal year end is the last Saturday in December.  \n    Intel Common stock CUSIP is 458140-10-0\n\n**When was Intel's initial public offering and the IPO price?**\n:   Intel went public October 13, 1971 at a price of USD 23.50 per share or 2 cents adjusted for our 13 subsequent stock splits.\n\n**What year and place was Intel Corporation incorporated?**\n:   Intel was incorporated 3/1/89 in Delaware. Below is the history from Intel California to the current Intel Delaware:\n\n    7/18/68 Incorporated: California, as NM Electronics Inc.  \n    8/6/68 Name changed to Intel Corporation, a California Corporation.  \n    3/1/89 Incorporation of Intel Corporation, a Delaware Corporation.  \n    5/5/89 Intel Corporation (California) merged with and into Intel Corporation (Delaware). Intel Corporation (Delaware) is the surviving corporation.\n\n**Who is Intel's accounting firm?**\n:   Ernst & Young LLP. They have been Intel's auditors since the company's inception in 1968.\n\n**Who is Intel's transfer agent?**\n:   Intel's Transfer agent is Computershare Investor Services LLC. Contact them for financial literature or stockholder services, to transfer stock, or to change your address. Current stockholders can get full portfolio access to their Intel Corporation account(s) by registering on the [Computershare Web site](https://www-us.computershare.com/Investor/?bhjs=1&fla=1&issuerid=scusintc&landing=y)\n\n    By Phone:  \n    In the U.S. tollfree: 1-800-298-0146  \n    Outside the U.S. direct dial: 1-312-360-5123  \n    Or by fax: 1-312-601-4332\n\n    By email:  \n    [web.queries@computershare.com](mailto:web.queries@computershare.com)\n\n    **By Regular Mail**  \n    Computershare  \n    PO Box 43078  \n    Providence, RI 02940-3078  \n    United States\n\n    **By Overnight Delivery**  \n    Computershare  \n    150 Royall Street  \n    Suite 101  \n    Canton, MA 02021  \n    United States\n\n**Is there an option to purchase and/or reinvest dividends in Intel shares directly?**\n:   Yes. Through [Computershare](https://www-us.computershare.com/Investor/DirectStock/Details?IssuerId=SCUSINTC&PlanId=SPP1&sv=t).\n\n**Where can I obtain Intel's quarterly reports?**\n:   Intel files quarterly reports (-Form 10-Q) with the SEC, which can be accessed [here](/filings-reports/all-sec-filings). We post the [earnings releases](/news-events/press-releases) and [quarterly financial statements](/financial-info/financial-results). The earnings release and Form 10Q are also available from [Computershare Investor Services LLC](https://www-us.computershare.com/Investor/3x/Plans/PlansList.asp?state=eStateDisplayPlanSummary&planid=221&cc=US&lang=en&bhjs=1&fla=1&theme=cpu) at 1-800-298-0146 or 1-312-360-5123 from other U.S. locations; outside the U.S. at 1-312-360-5123.\n\n**How can I reach the Investor Relations Department?**\n:   For other investor inquiries or to contact someone in our Investor Relations department, please contact us at:\n\n    Intel Corporation  \n    RNB 4-148  \n    2200 Mission College Blvd  \n    Santa Clara, California 95054  \n    USA\n\n    Phone: 1-408-765-1480\n\n    [Investor.Relations@intel.com](mailto:Investor.Relations@intel.com)\n\n**When was Intel's stockholder meeting?**\n:   Information about Intel’s most recent Annual Stockholders’ Meeting can be found [here](/news-events/annual-stockholders-meeting).\n\n* [Email Alerts](/news-events/email-alerts)\n* [Tear Sheet](https://d1io3yog0oux5.cloudfront.net/_88b01b330621eb4afbd070d5caa4f035/intel/files/Tear+Sheet.pdf \"Tear Sheet\")\n* [Contacts](/about-intel/contacts)\n* [RSS News Feed](https://www.intc.com/news-events/press-releases/rss)\n\nMarket Data copyright © 2026 [QuoteMedia](http://www.quotemedia.com). Data delayed 15 minutes unless otherwise indicated (view [delay times](http://www.quotemedia.com/legal/tos/#times) for all exchanges). RT=Real-Time, EOD=End of Day, PD=Previous Day. Market Data powered by [QuoteMedia](http://www.quotemedia.com). [Terms of Use](http://www.quotemedia.com/legal/tos/).\n\n ", "id": "3c38e7-02"}, {"url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intel", "title": "Intel - Wikipedia", "score": 0.7440808, "raw_content": "[Jump to content](#bodyContent)\n\n[![](/static/images/icons/enwiki-25.svg)  ![Wikipedia](/static/images/mobile/copyright/wikipedia-wordmark-en-25.svg) ![The Free Encyclopedia](/static/images/mobile/copyright/wikipedia-tagline-en-25.svg)](/wiki/Main_Page)\n\n[Search](/wiki/Special:Search \"Search Wikipedia [f]\")\n\n## Contents\n\n* [1 History](#History)\n  + [1.1 Origins](#Origins)\n  + [1.2 Early history](#Early_history)\n  + [1.3 Challenges to dominance (2000s)](#Challenges_to_dominance_(2000s))\n    - [1.3.1 Litigation](#Litigation)\n  + [1.4 Reorganization and success with Intel Core (2005–2015)](#Reorganization_and_success_with_Intel_Core_(2005–2015))\n    - [1.4.1 Attempts at entering the smartphone market](#Attempts_at_entering_the_smartphone_market)\n    - [1.4.2 Intel custom foundry](#Intel_custom_foundry)\n  + [1.5 Security and manufacturing challenges (2016–2021)](#Security_and_manufacturing_challenges_(2016–2021))\n    - [1.5.1 10 nm process node issues](#10_nm_process